# Generated by LFGitignore - https://lfgitignore.com
# Created: 2025-08-01 14:32:42 UTC
# Technologies: Python
#
# Every directory rule below is root-anchored (`/name/`), because an unanchored
# `name/` matches that directory at *any* depth - including under `src/`, where a
# frontend or Rust source directory of that name would be silently untrackable.
# The failure is silent and total: `git add src` commits zero files and reports
# success, `git status` shows nothing, and ESLint (via `includeIgnoreFile`) and
# Prettier both skip the subtree, so every gate reads green with the whole feature
# missing.
#
# `__pycache__/` and `node_modules/` are the deliberate exceptions and stay
# unanchored: a directory by either name is by definition generated output, never
# source, so shadowing cannot hide anything worth tracking, and a nested instance
# of either is still junk.

